WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.602
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:04.803
Thanks for watching again.

00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:06.405
Let's get to some
news and jokes.

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:08.308
Well, guys, this was big today.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:12.044
The C.E.O.s of Facebook, Amazon,
Apple, and Google

00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:14.347
all testified before
a House subcommittee

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.950
over accusations that
they've stifled competition

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.351
in their industry.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.421
That's them
testifying right there.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.689
Yep, seeing the four of them
together was like

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:27.960
the Beatles of selling your
personal[ information.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.698
[ British accent ]
I am the walrus. I am you.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:35.068
I have all your baby photos.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.436
[ Normal voice ] I don't like to
pass judgment,

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.637
but these guys made the cast of
"The Big Bang Theory"

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:40.773
look like "The Avengers."

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.775
It was basically like the
Super Bowl of guys

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:45.712
who were picked last in sports.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.480
It was not an easy day
for lawmakers.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.250
They were like, "I'd grill you,
but I need Amazon to survive,

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.786
Google knows my search history,
Apple's got my texts,

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.321
and Facebook's got
my drunk pics.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.957
So we're good."

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.693
That's right -- a bunch of
tech C.E.O.s testified

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.995
for hours over videoconference.

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:05.064
So if you thought yesterday's
William Barr testimony

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.532
was exciting, then...

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:09.569
[ Snores ]

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.138
Yeah, the hearing was
a little dull.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:15.374
While Jeff Bezos was testifying,
a graphic popped up that said,

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:16.809
"People who have viewed
this testimony

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.978
also viewed paint drying."

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.217
Yeah, because of coronavirus,

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:27.153
the four men testified
via videoconference.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.654
It's too bad they
didn't do it in person,

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:30.022
because they could have rolled
up together in this --

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:36.663
the Geek Squad clown car.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.698
I'm not sure these guys
like each other,

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.466
because to get on
Mark Zuckerberg's nerves,

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:43.169
all the other C.E.O.s
made their background this.

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:47.139
This was actually
Mark Zuckerberg's

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:49.275
fourth time
testifying before Congress,

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.443
but you could also say that
Zuckerberg has testified

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:52.612
900 times.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:55.014
It doesn't matter.
He won't fact-check it.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:58.617
At one point during the hearing,
Congressman Jim Sensenbrenner

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:01.120
questioned Zuckerberg about how
Donald Trump Jr.'s

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.424
Twitter account was suspended,
and it was a little awkward.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:05.458
Watch this.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.594 line:0%
-It was reported that
Donald Trump Jr.

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:11.397 line:0%
got taken down
for a period of time

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.399 line:0%
because he put something up,

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:17.203 line:0%
the efficacy of
hydroxychloroquine.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:20.472 line:0%
Why did that happen?

00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:22.308 line:0%
-Congressman, well,
first, to be clear,

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.677 line:0%
I think you might be referring
to happened on Twitter,

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:29.182 line:0%
so it's hard for me
to speak to that.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:33.986
-The Congressman was like,
"Um, what's the difference?"

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:36.555
Then the Congressman was like,
"Twitter. Right, right.

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:40.226
So that question is for you,
Jeff Bezos."

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.128
But it was a big day
on Capitol Hill,

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.962
with all the most
important leaders in tech

00:02:43.962 --> 00:02:45.498
appearing to testify.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.667
Here's what they had to say
before things got started.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.536
First, Apple C.E.O.
Tim Cook said...

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.207
Then Facebook C.E.O.
Mark Zuckerberg said...

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.810
Then Amazon's Jeff Bezos said...

00:03:00.145 --> 00:03:02.782
Then Clippy, the
Microsoft paper clip said...

00:03:10.088 --> 00:03:11.424
Then Tim Cook said...

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.028
Then Clippy said...

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.670
Then Zuckerberg said...

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:27.307
And then Clippy said...

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.280
Then Cook said...

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.383
And Clippy said...

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:47.960
Well, guys, President Trump held
another coronavirus briefing

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.263
last night, or,
as they're now being called,

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:52.899
"The Crazy Uncle on
Facebook Hour."

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.934
During the briefing,
Trump defended the doctor

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.770
he re-tweeted the other night,
who said things like

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.606
some health issues
are caused by having sex dreams

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.541
about demons and witches.

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:05.644
Yeah. Trump actually called
her impressive.

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:08.881
Trump was like, "Of all
the demon-sex doctors out there,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.083
she's the best.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:15.988
She's rated 10 out of 10
on WebMDemon."

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.491
WebMDemon. Yeah.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:19.825
At this point, Trump thinks

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:21.361
anyone in a white coat
is a doctor.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:22.861
This morning,
he was watching "Miami Vice"

00:04:22.861 --> 00:04:25.164
and was taking notes.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.666
It's like Trump is an actor
doing a one-man show,

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:29.702
and his staff are his friends,
who have to be like,

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.905
"That was...good.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:35.140
Interesting choices.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.243
Yeah. Yeah.
I think what she said.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:39.111
Interesting.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.380
It was interesting and good.
Good and interesting.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.116
You pick the order."

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:45.985
When another reporter asked
Trump a question

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.387
about Dr. Fauci, he seemed to
take it kind of personally.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:49.489
Listen to this.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:51.357
-So, it sort of is curious.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:54.427
A man works for us, with us,
very closely, Dr. Fauci --

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:57.964
and Dr. Birx,
also highly thought of --

00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:00.900
and, yet, they're highly thought
of, but nobody likes me.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.202
It can only be my personality.
That's all.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.140
-And then Trump waited
30 minutes

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.676
for someone to say, "No, no,
we love you."

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:11.911
Actually,
right after he said that,

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.813
a voice was heard through a
speaker saying,

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:14.914
[ Russian accent ]
"Not true, Donald.

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:19.052
I still love you."
[ Laughs ]

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.352
Did you guys see this yesterday?

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:22.221
When Joe Biden
was at a campaign event,

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:25.057
someone took a photo of
the notes he had in his hand,

00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:26.492
and many people think
it might have tipped

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.227
who he's picking as his V.P.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.029
Check it out. Yeah.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.764
It says "Kamala Harris"
and then has a bunch

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.833
of compliments about
her underneath.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.801
Yeah. Trump had a
similar thing happen to him

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:37.303
at yesterday's COVID briefing

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.138
when someone took a photo
of his notes.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.707 line:0%
It says...

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:53.419
Let's get to some business news.

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:55.288
I read that Budweiser
is releasing

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.990
its first-ever
alcohol-free beer,

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.525
called Budweiser Zero.

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.393
Check it out.

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:04.864
Yeah. Well, they're already
testing out some slogans.

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:07.166
First, there's
"Budweiser Zero --

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:11.104
your friends will still
worry about you."

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:13.205
Next up, there is,
"Budweiser Zero --

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:15.474
when you want all your
conversations at the party

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:18.344
to be, "So..."

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:22.181
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:25.751
Yeah, you got that.
You got that, yeah?

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:27.119
And, of course, last, there is

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:30.122
"Budweiser Zero --
basically Coors Light."

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:31.590
All good options.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:33.992
And, finally, some good news
to cheer everyone up.

00:06:33.992 --> 00:06:35.160
Check this out.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.796 line:0%
-A 99-year-old woman
in California

00:06:37.796 --> 00:06:40.999 line:0%
is now the world's oldest
flight instructor.

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:43.769 line:0%
Robina Asti gave her
final flight lesson,

00:06:43.769 --> 00:06:46.505 line:0%
and she says she wants to show
that people her age

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:51.577 line:0%
are strong, vital, and have
something to contribute.

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:57.784
-Oh my God.
I think we found Amelia Earhart.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:04.223
All of her flights
start the same way --

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:07.727
backing the plane out of the
gate and running over a mailbox.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.463
When asked who taught her,
she said,

00:07:11.463 --> 00:07:15.334
"Two nice young boys --
Orville and Wilbur."

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.102
It's a little worrisome
when you get up in the air

00:07:17.102 --> 00:07:18.403
and she looks at you and says,

00:07:18.403 --> 00:07:20.706
"I've always wanted to take
flying lessons."

